// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Logical model — retail point-of-sale, 3NF.
//
// What belongs here: entities, their attributes, keys, and relationships, in
// third normal form. This is the logical phase: it comes after docs/conceptual.md
// is agreed and before any migration is written. The DDL in migrations/ is
// derived from this file, never the reverse.
//
// Done when: every entity in docs/conceptual.md appears here with attributes and
// a key; every relationship has an explicit Ref with cardinality; every table
// and column has a Note; 3NF holds with no transitive dependency anyone has to
// defend; and every business term used matches docs/glossary.md exactly.
//
// Must NOT go here: Postgres-specific types, indexes, partitions, tablespaces,
// storage parameters, or anything about performance — those are physical, they
// live in the migration. No facts, no dimensions, no star schemas, ever: this is
// the source system.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Conventions
//
// Naming
//   tables            singular, snake_case, business language: transaction_line
//                     not TransactionLines, not txn_ln
//   columns           snake_case; no table-name prefix (transaction.id, not
//                     transaction.transaction_id)
//   primary key       id
//   foreign key       <referenced_table>_id
//   booleans          is_ / has_ prefix
//   timestamps        _at suffix (system time); dates _date suffix (business time)
//   money             amount / _amount suffix, with the currency stated in a Note
//   no abbreviations  qty, txn, cust, amt are all rejected in review
//   reserved words    never used as identifiers, not even quoted
//
// Types (logical, not Postgres)
//   text, integer, decimal(p,s), boolean, date, timestamp, uuid
//   Map to Postgres in the migration, not here.
//
// Notes
//   Every table and every column carries a Note. The Note text is what becomes
//   the COMMENT ON in the migration — write it once, here, and carry it across.
//   A column whose Note only restates its name is not documented.
//
// Relationships
//   One Ref per relationship, cardinality explicit (>, <, -, <>). Resolve
//   many-to-many with a named associative entity that has its own business
//   meaning — if you cannot name it in business language, the relationship is
//   wrong.
//
// Enums
//   Use an Enum only for a closed set the business controls and rarely changes.
//   Anything a store manager can add to is a lookup table, not an Enum.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Project retail_oltp {
  database_type: 'PostgreSQL'
  Note: 'Source system for retail point-of-sale. 3NF OLTP. Not a warehouse.'
}

// No entities yet — the conceptual phase is not finished.
